"],"criteria":["T7","T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'This story establishes the one-parser contract and safe canonical help'","'54 hand-maintained package-help files, and 22 curated intercept descriptions'","Absence: no ADR/AGENTS.md/design-doc mention anywhere in Approach, Testing, or Acceptance Criteria for the new parser/registry contract"],"finding":"The plan introduces a novel architectural contract (single-source argparse factories, frozen route records, a factory protocol, registry validation, and generated canonical help superseding 54 hand-maintained help files) but names no ADR, AGENTS.md, or design-doc update capturing this one-parser contract decision.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc84ef99338805917","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"nb3cc87ae900cd017","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Future contributors add a new command via imperative parsing because the one-parser contract is documented only implicitly in generated artifacts","The 54 replaced help files or 22 intercept descriptions leave stale references in docs that pointed at hand-maintained sources"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how a pure factory becomes the runtime parser for families whose rejection diagnostics differ from argparse's default: state whether the factory owns rejection (accepting a diagnostic-normalization delta as an approved public change) or whether a thin factory-driven unknown-option check that reproduces the bespoke bytes is permitted, and reconcile that rule with the anti-imperative prohibition and AC-5.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'Factories … return argparse parsers used by runtime handlers'","Approach: 'leaving runtime on an imperative parser after adding a factory is prohibited'","AC-5: 'Parser parity tests show no unapproved delta in accepted/rejected argv, --, diagnostics, streams, or exit codes'","Code evidence (src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/reads.py docstring): 'the runtime handlers keep their bespoke unknown-option diagnostics (Error: unknown option, next-batch's Unknown flag, validate's Unknown option) and exit codes'; factories built add_help=False/allow_abbrev=False model only the ACCEPTED grammar"],"finding":"The plan's Approach mandates that each migrated runtime handler consume its factory and prohibits 'leaving runtime on an imperative parser after adding a factory', while AC-5 requires no diagnostic/exit-code delta; but for families whose runtime rejection diagnostics differ from argparse's default (e.g. read commands emit bespoke 'Error: unknown option' / 'Unknown flag' / 'Unknown option' rather than argparse's usage+error), the plan does not specify how the pure factory becomes the runtime parser without either (a) changing those diagnostics or (b) retaining an imperative unknown-option scan alongside the factory. This leaves the migration mechanism under-specified for the exact case where the single-parser contract and the parity contract are in tension.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdaf51f25ab3e7959","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (\"return argparse parsers used by runtime handlers\", \"leaving runtime on an imperative parser after adding a factory is prohibited\") vs AC-5 and AC-1","norm_id":"n61a412c1aa0f9cf5","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A read-family handler keeps its own unknown-option scan to preserve 'Error: unknown option' bytes, so the factory drives only accepted-argv parsing and the rejection path is still imperative — arguably violating the anti-imperative prohibition while satisfying parity.","A reviewer/implementer treats 'runtime-used factory' as requiring argparse to own rejection, changing diagnostics and breaking AC-5."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make `metrics` ownership explicit in S2c (name it as a migrated advanced family in its Approach and acceptance criteria) so S2b's exclusion has a definite owner and no owned-by-none gap exists during parallel execution.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["S2b AC1/Approach: 'EXCLUDE `metrics`: its route already carries `parser_factory=\"rebar._cli._parsers.advanced.metrics:build\"` from S2c and is out of scope here (re-migrating it is forbidden).'","S2c Approach family list: 'Families include bridge and reconcile, audit, prompt/criteria/LLM setup, review/scan/explain/sign operations, workflow, config/identity verification/trusted-environment/remote-certificate commands, and enrichment.' — `metrics` is named only in the negative import-blocker list ('no ... metrics ... imports'), never as a family it migrates.","S2c roster AC: 'Every registered advanced command and nested subcommand runtime uses one S2a parser factory' — does not explicitly enumerate `metrics`.","Parent Approach: 'Core and advanced migrations may proceed in parallel after the foundation.'","container pairing: parent + a8ce-8ffa-54d7-432f/b2ff-03f7-a223-4900/cd12-2815-d2ab-430a/eb0d-4c3d-5344-47d7"],"finding":"S2b's exclusion of `metrics` rests on a cross-child assumption that S2c has already migrated it (`its route already carries parser_factory=\"rebar._cli._parsers.advanced.metrics:build\" from S2c`), but S2c's Approach family list and its roster acceptance criteria never claim `metrics` as a migrated advanced family. Combined with the parent's statement that core and advanced migrations 'may proceed in parallel after the foundation', during the parallel window `metrics` can be owned by NEITHER child — S2b forbids re-migrating it and S2c does not name it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fae2c4590d3ef21bc","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child eb0d-4c3d-5344-47d7 (S2b) and child a8ce-8ffa-54d7-432f (S2c)","norm_id":"n87cd61a57da92afe","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["S2b lands (or is planned) before S2c actually migrates metrics: the metrics route has no `parser_factory` yet, S2b's exclusion leaves it unmigrated, and parent AC1 ('every registered command grammar is produced by one runtime-used side-effect-free argparse factory') fails at story roll-up because no child owns metrics.","Reviewer of S2c cannot confirm metrics is in scope from S2c's own AC text, so an S2c executor may reasonably omit it, matching S2b's forbidden re-migration into an owned-by-none gap."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add `metrics` to S2c's advanced family list and to its AC1 enumeration (or add an explicit note in S2c that it owns the `rebar._cli._parsers.advanced.metrics:build` factory that S2b depends on), so the S2b/S2c handoff is symmetric rather than one-sided.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"b852477d8830ea10","material_parts":{"children":["5177062d108dac38",4],"description":["ad0dfb8eb